CREATE A PYTHON PROGRAM TO AUTOMATE LOGIN TO A WEBSITE USING SELENIUM

AIM

To create a python program to automate login to a website using Selenium.

ALGORITHM

Step 1: Start the program

Step 2: Create an HTML webpage (index.html) containing a login form with username,

password, and login button.

Step 3: Import required modules (webdriver, By from selenium, and time).

Step 4: Launch the Chrome browser using WebDriver

= webdriver.Chrome()

Step 5: Open the local webpage URL using driver.get().

driver.get("http://localhost:8000")

Step 6: Find username and password input elements by ID and enter credentials using

send keys()

driver.find_element(By.ID, "username").send_keys("student123")

driver.find_element(By.ID, "password").send_keys("pass123")

Step 7: Find the login button by ID and trigger submission using elick().

driver.find_element(By. ID, "login-button").click()

Step 8: Wait to view the login result, quit the browser session, and stop the program.

PROGRAM

index.html:

<!DOCTYPE html>

<title>Student Login</title>

<style>

body { display: grid; place-content: center; height: 100vh;, font-family: system-ui; }

form { display: grid; gap: 8px; width: 240px; }

